#!/usr/bin/env perl
# PODNAME: robocop
# ABSTRACT: OCP robocop controller (in-cluster worker management)

use strict;
use warnings;
use FindBin;
use lib "$FindBin::Bin/../lib";

our $VERSION = '0.001';
use OCP::Robocop;
use OCP::Robocop::Controller;

# The Deployment starts this as `robocop controller` (share/robocop/deployment.yaml).
# That argument used to fall on the floor: bin/robocop ran OCP::Robocop->run
# unconditionally, which blocks on the disabled port-9999 key-injection stub and
# never reaches the reconciliation controller (karr #33). Read @ARGV and route
# the `controller` subcommand to OCP::Robocop::Controller, built from the
# environment; every other invocation keeps the legacy OCP::Robocop behaviour.
if (@ARGV && $ARGV[0] eq 'controller') {
    my $controller = OCP::Robocop::Controller->from_env;
    $controller->run;
} else {
    my $robocop = OCP::Robocop->new;
    $robocop->run;
}

__END__

=head1 NAME

robocop - OCP Kubernetes controller for worker management

=head1 SYNOPSIS

    # Reconciliation controller (how the Deployment starts it)
    robocop controller

    # Legacy key-injection entry point (no subcommand)
    robocop

=head1 DESCRIPTION

Robocop is the in-cluster controller that manages worker nodes automatically.
This script is the entry point for the robocop Deployment in Kubernetes.

The first argument selects the mode:

=over 4

=item B<controller>

Builds an L<OCP::Robocop::Controller> from the environment (via
C<< OCP::Robocop::Controller->from_env >>) and watches OCPNode custom resources,
reconciling each through L<OCP::Node>. This is the command the Deployment runs
(C<share/robocop/deployment.yaml>).

=item I<(no argument)>

The legacy L<OCP::Robocop> path: waits for robo-ssh key injection, keeps the key
in memory only, and CRIU-checkpoints itself. The injector (C<ocp inject-key>)
needs C<port_forward> and is currently disabled (see karr #2), so this path
blocks until that is redeemed or removed.

=back

=head1 ENVIRONMENT

The B<controller> subcommand reads its configuration from the environment:

=over 4

=item B<ROBO_SSH_KEY> (required)

The robo-key private key material, used to reach freshly provisioned workers.

=item B<RKE2_SERVER_URL> (required)

The RKE2/K3s server (join) URL, e.g. C<https://police1:9345>.

=item B<RKE2_TOKEN> (required)

The node join token.

=item B<NAMESPACE> (optional)

Namespace to watch; defaults to C<ocp-system>. Set from the pod's
C<metadata.namespace> in the Deployment.

=item B<OCP_DISTRIBUTION> (optional)

C<rke2> (default) or C<k3s>.

=item B<CHECKPOINT_DIR>

Legacy path only: directory for CRIU checkpoints (default: /dev/shm/robocop).

=back

A missing required variable is fatal, with the offending name reported on
STDERR.

=head1 SEE ALSO

L<OCP::Robocop::Controller>, L<OCP::Robocop>

=cut
